WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.400
"Eye of newt, toe of frog,
wool of bat, and tongue of dog."

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:11.220
Those are four of the ingredients used
by the witches in Shakespeare's ... Scottish play.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:17.620
See, the thing is, I am currently very much on the stage,
on a set, here at the Warner Brothers Studio tour.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.620
This is the potions classroom from Harry Potter.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:27.980
and well, it's considered extremely bad luck to use
'that word', 'that name', on an actual set.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:32.260
It is said that Shakespeare used an actual witches brew

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:38.480
and witches suitably angered by that
placed a curse on the play, or on him

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:42.380
or, if you believe it, on anyone who said that word.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:48.140
and the result is that saying "M...th" here,
is considered a very bad idea

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:50.820
but did you ever think about that.
That doesn't really make sense

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:53.680
I mean, not the curse part.
That obviously doesn't make sense

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:57.200
but the fact that witches would use eye of newt.

00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:01.380
Witches, the cunning folk,
as they were called, the herbalists.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.600
They didn't get newts and cut out bits of their eyes
and put them in a potion.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.600
That doesn't make any sense.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:12.940
Actually, they used herbs and botanicals,
and that's what "eye of newt" actually was.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:17.280
"Eye of newt" is just a code word
for something much more innocuous.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:20.940
and there are any number of reasons why
that might have been. The true reason is lost to history

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:26.280
It could have been a code word, designed
to keep magic within the... well, the "magic circle".

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.640
Or it might just have been
a dialectal thing, we don't know

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:33.920
but what we do know, "eye of newt"
was actually just mustard seed,

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.960
something warm and calming to add to a healing broth,

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:39.560
something you might not have known.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:40.060
STUPIFY!

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:40.900
EXPELLIARMUS!

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:42.900
...amateurs.

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:46.480
I'm currently at the Harry Potter Studios tour

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:52.980
and this is most definitely a sound stage, which means
it would be very bad luck... for me to say... the

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:55.020
...hi.

